course: dictionary
lesson: 14089
title: Megaphone: making your voice carry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A megaphone is a cone-shaped tool you speak into to make your voice louder, so a crowd can hear you. «The coach used a megaphone to call the runners to the start line.» The clue is the crowd at a sports day: the coach needed to be heard across a big space.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The lifeguard used a megaphone to warn the swimmers.» If you put "a loud, cone-shaped voice tool" in its place, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Sometimes a word is used in a figurative way, meaning something other than the tool itself. «Her blog became a megaphone for her ideas.» A blog cannot be shouted into, so the clue tells you that a megaphone here is something that helps her message reach many people.
fact: A megaphone is a cone-shaped device you speak into to make your voice louder.
fact: A megaphone helps a crowd hear you, for example at sports days, protests, beaches and fire drills.
fact: Modern megaphones use batteries and are electric.
fact: Figuratively, a megaphone is something that helps a person spread their message widely.
fact: Never shout into someone's ear with a megaphone, because very loud sound can damage hearing.
exercise: «The sports day teacher used a megaphone so every class could hear the rules.» What is a megaphone used for? | To cook food on the beach | To make music quieter | *To make a voice louder so a crowd can hear | To keep the rain off the grass
exercise: Sam wants to tell the whole school about the fire drill at once. Which tool should he use? | A pencil | A calculator | *A megaphone | A pair of socks
exercise: «Her blog became a megaphone for her ideas, reaching thousands of readers.» In this sentence, what does megaphone mean? | *Something that helps a person spread their message widely | A loud noise from a broken car | A kind of musical instrument | A small torch
test: In science, what does a cone-shaped megaphone do to sound? | *Directs sound forward so the voice carries further | Makes the sound travel backwards into your own ear | Stops all sound from getting out | Turns sound into light
test: «Never shout into someone's ear with a megaphone.» Why is this a rule? | The ear is too small to fit | The megaphone will break | *Very loud sound can damage hearing | It uses too many batteries
exam: «The leader used megaphone diplomacy, shouting her messages publicly rather than talking quietly with each group.» What does megaphone diplomacy mean? | *Shouting messages publicly rather than talking privately | Having a quiet, private talk with everyone | Writing letters to the newspaper | Playing music loudly at a party
